      "description": "# Hack With GDG S4\n\n### 36 Hours of Innovation, Building, and Impact\n\n**Hack With GDG S4** is the fourth season of the flagship hackathon organized by **Google Developer Groups – KSR College of Engineering (GDG KSRCE)**. The event brings together developers, designers, innovators, and problem-solvers to transform ideas into impactful solutions through technology.\n\n## Important Update\n\nDue to unforeseen circumstances, **Hack With GDG S4 has been postponed**.\n\n**The revised dates for the hackathon will be announced soon.**\n\nParticipants are requested to follow our official communication channels for updates regarding the new schedule, submission deadlines, and other event-related announcements.\n\n## Event Structure\n\n### Round 1 — Ideation & Selection\n\nParticipants will submit their **project idea in PPT/PDF format** for evaluation.\n\nTeams will be evaluated based on their problem statement, proposed solution, innovation, feasibility, and potential impact. A working prototype is not mandatory at this stage, but prior technical work may be considered an advantage.\n\nSelected teams will advance to the offline hackathon.\n\n### Round 2 — The Hack\n\nSelected teams will participate in a **36-hour offline hackathon**, where they will build and demonstrate their solutions on-site.\n\nParticipants will have access to:\n\n* Industry mentorship\n* Technical guidance\n* Networking opportunities\n* Side events and activities\n* Meals and refreshments throughout the event\n\n## Who Can Participate?\n\nHack With GDG S4 welcomes participants across different skill levels and backgrounds.\n\n* **Developers** — Build and implement innovative solutions\n* **Designers** — Create engaging and user-friendly experiences\n* **Innovators** — Identify real-world problems and develop meaningful solutions\n\n**Team Size:** 1–4 members\n\nBoth **beginners and experienced participants** are welcome to participate.\n\n## Themes & Innovation\n\nThe hackathon follows an **Open Innovation** approach. Participants are encouraged to identify meaningful real-world problems and develop technology-driven solutions across diverse domains.\n\n## Rewards & Recognition\n\n🏆 **Cash prizes** for winning teams\n📜 **Participation certificates** for attendees\n🤝 **Mentorship and networking opportunities**\n💡 **Hands-on experience building solutions in a 36-hour environment**\n\n## Venue\n\n**KSR College of Engineering**\nNamakkal, Tamil Nadu, India\n\n**Event Format:** Offline\n**Duration:** 36 Hours\n**Dates:** **To be announced**\n\n## Contact\n\nFor queries and further information:\n\n**Email:** [gdgksrce@gmail.com](mailto:gdgksrce@gmail.com)\n**Instagram:** @gdg_ksrce\n\n### Stay Tuned\n\nThe **revised event dates and updated schedule will be announced soon**. Participants are encouraged to stay connected with GDG KSRCE for the latest announcements.",
