      "description": "HAXFINITY — Hack the Infinite\n\nThe 24-hour hackathon of XTHRON '26\n\n December 2026\nAmal College of Advanced Studies (Autonomous), Nilambur, Kerala\nPrize Pool: Exciting prizes\nTeam Size: 2–4 participants\n\nBuild real solutions. Solve meaningful problems. Create something that works.\n\nHAXFINITY is the 24-hour hackathon conducted as part of XTHRON '26, the annual IT fest of the Department of Computer Science, Amal College of Advanced Studies (Autonomous), Nilambur.\n\nFor 24 hours, students from different colleges and backgrounds will come together to identify problems, develop  software solutions, build working prototypes, and present their ideas to a panel of judges.\n\nThere is no compulsory theme. Participants are free to choose a problem and develop a software solution using any suitable technology.\n\nWhether you are an experienced developer or participating in your first hackathon, HAXFINITY is a space to learn, collaborate, experiment, and build.\n\nPRIZE POOL — Exciting prizes\n\n\nTRACKS\n\nOPEN INNOVATION\n\nBuild anything that solves a real problem.\n\nYou may work in education, healthcare, finance, agriculture, entertainment, productivity, cybersecurity, accessibility, sustainability, or any other domain.\n\nThere is no fixed problem statement and no restriction on technology. Choose a problem, design a solution, build a working prototype, and surprise the judges.\n\nAI / ML\n\nBuild intelligent systems using machine learning, generative AI, natural language processing, computer vision, recommendation systems, data analysis, or any other AI-related technology.\n\nProjects will be evaluated on technical implementation, originality, usefulness, and real-world applicability.\n\nSOCIAL GOOD\n\nBuild technology that improves people’s lives.\n\nPossible areas include rural development, accessibility, mental health, financial inclusion, education, healthcare, environmental protection, and community welfare.\n\nProjects in this track will be evaluated on impact, usability, sustainability, and the effectiveness of the proposed solution.\n\nWHAT THE HACKATHON LOOKS LIKE\n\n16 December, 10:30 AM — Opening ceremony and problem-solving begins.\n\nDuring the day — Teams form, ideas take shape, and development begins.\n\nThroughout the event — Mentoring, technical support, checkpoints, and interaction with fellow participants.\n\nMidnight — The hackathon continues with snacks, discussions, debugging, and late-night building.\n\n17 December, 10:32 AM — Submission deadline and code freeze.\n\nAfter submission — Teams prepare their final demonstrations.\n\nFinal judging — Each team presents its working prototype to the judges.\n\nClosing ceremony — Winners are announced and prizes are distributed.\n\nWHO CAN PARTICIPATE?\n\nHAXFINITY is open to students from all streams and colleges.\n\nStudents from computer science, information technology, engineering, science, commerce, management, design, and other disciplines are welcome.\n\nYou may participate if you are:\n\n- A beginner attending your first hackathon.\n- An experienced developer.\n- A designer or creative problem-solver.\n- A student interested in AI, cybersecurity, cloud, web, mobile, or social-impact technology.\n- Someone with an idea and the willingness to build it.\n\nThe only requirement is that you come prepared to learn, collaborate, and create.\n\nTEAM DETAILS\n\n- Each team must have 2–4 participants.\n- Solo participation is not permitted.\n- Participants from different colleges may form one team.\n- Participants from different academic streams may form one team.\n- Interdisciplinary teams are encouraged.\n- Each participant may be part of only one team.\n\nWHERE IT HAPPENS\n\nAmal College of Advanced Studies (Autonomous)\nSanthigramam, Eranhimangad\nNilambur, Malappuram, Kerala — 679329\n\nThe campus is located in the Nilambur region of Kerala, known for its natural surroundings and teak forests.\n\nThe college is approximately:\n\n- 3 km from Nilambur Railway Station.\n- 1 km from the Calicut–Nilambur–Ooty highway.\n\nTravel and accommodation information will be shared with registered participants.\n\nWHAT WE PROVIDE\n\n- Dedicated workspace for participating teams.\n- Power and internet access.\n- Lunch on the first day.\n- Dinner on the first day.\n- Breakfast on the second day.\n- Midnight snacks.\n- Technical assistance during the event.\n- Mentoring and guidance, subject to mentor availability.\n- Certificates for participants.\n- A platform to demonstrate projects to judges and fellow innovators.\n\nCloud credits, software benefits, and additional resources may be announced later if they are officially confirmed.\n\nRULES\n\n- Teams must contain 2–4 participants.\n- The project must be developed during the official hackathon period.\n- Participants may use open-source libraries, frameworks, APIs, and publicly available datasets.\n- Previously developed projects may not be submitted as new work.\n- Teams must clearly disclose any pre-existing code, templates, datasets, APIs, or third-party services used.\n- Projects must be submitted through Devfolio before the deadline.\n- Late submissions may not be accepted.\n- A working prototype or meaningful demonstration is expected.\n- Teams must be prepared to explain their technology, development process, and contribution.\n- Projects must not violate copyright, privacy, security, or applicable law.\n- All participants must follow the event Code of Conduct.\n- The organisers reserve the right to reject projects that are unsafe, copied, offensive, illegal, or unrelated to the event.\n- The detailed judging criteria and final rules will be published before the event.\n\n\n\n\nHAXFINITY — Hack the Infinite\nEXTHRONE ’26\n12–13 December 2026",
