      "description": "# GeNarrative Clash 2026\n*Where Generative AI Meets Human Creativity*\n\nAre you ready to redefine how stories are told, music is composed, and digital art is created? **GeNarrative Clash** is Kolkata's premier Prompt Engineering & AI Building Challenge, organized by the GeeksforGeeks Student Chapter at Techno India University.\n\n---\n\n### 🚀 Hands-On AI & API Masterclass (Included!)\nDon't worry if you are new to AI development! Before the live challenge kicks off, every participant gets access to an exclusive **1-Hour Hands-On Masterclass on AI Development & API Integration**. Learn how to harness cutting-edge LLMs, query GenAI APIs, and leverage rapid prototyping tools so you can build a solid, production-ready product with confidence.\n\n---\n\n### 🎁 Perks, Bounties & Swag\n* **Cash Bounties & Prize Pool:** Generous rewards or prizes for top-performing teams and winners.\n* **Exclusive Swags:** Official sponsor goodies for top 12 finalists.\n* **Certificates for All:** Official certificates of participation and achievement for all attending hackers.\n\n---\n\n### 🎨 The Challenge: Empowering the Creative Artist (Open Track)\nGenerative AI shouldn't replace human creators, it should supercharge them! **GeNarrative Clash** features an Open Track focused on building real-world solutions that assist, elevate, and support creative artists in their work. \n\nYou are free to solve any real-world problem in the artistic or creative domain.\n\n**Inspiration & Potential Project Directions:**\n* **Storytelling & Narrative Assistants:** GenAI co-writers that help authors outline complex multiverses, generate dynamic dialogue, or build interactive narratives.\n* **AI Music & Sound Studios:** Production-ready suites that assist musicians with harmonies, stem generation, or intelligent sound design.\n* **Autonomous Creator Agents:** GenAI agents and social media co-pilots that help digital creators manage, format, and schedule content tailored to their target audience.\n* **Digital Art & Visual Co-Pilots:** Tools that aid animators, illustrators, and designers in concept generation and workflow automation.\n\n---\n\n### ⚙️ Hackathon Rules & Technical Freedom\n* **No Tech Stack Restrictions:** You are completely free to use any programming language, framework, API, or LLM (OpenAI, Claude, open-source models, or leading AI APIs).\n* **The 50/50 Pre-Building Rule:** To ensure high-quality, production-ready submissions, teams are permitted to pre-build up to **50% of their project before event day** (wireframes, boilerplate code, trained prompts, or baseline UI). The remaining **50% of the project must be built live** during the 6-hour hacking sprint.\n\n---\n\n### 📍 Venue & Event Date\n* **Date:** November 21, 2026  \n* **Venue:** Techno India University, EM Block, Sector V, Salt Lake, Kolkata, West Bengal 700091",
