      "description": "**Q-Hack India 2026** is a national-level quantum hackathon hosted by QuantumRIT at Ramaiah Institute of Technology, Bengaluru, as part of [Quantum Week](https://www.quantumweek.tech/) 2026, a IBM Qiskit Fall Fest program.\n\nThe hackathon brings together students, developers, researchers and quantum enthusiasts to explore real-world applications of quantum computing. Participants will move from idea to prototype through a competitive build experience, with access to mentorship, technical resources and a platform to showcase their work.\n\nWhether you are new to quantum computing or an expert, the challenge is designed to encourage experimentation, practical problem-solving and ambitious ideas.\n\n**Hackathon at a Glance**\n**Format:** 2 Rounds + Grand Finale\n**Team Size:** 3–4 members \n**Eligibility:** Undergraduate & Postgraduate Students\n**Location:** Online + In-person Finale at Ramaiah Institute of Technology, Bengaluru\n\n**Round 1 —** Idea & Prototype Submission 27 Sep – 10 Oct 2026\n**Round 2 —** Enhancement Sprint 12 – 29 Oct 2026\n**Grand Finale:** 30–31 Oct 2026 \n\n\n**Tracks**\nQuantum Biotech & Chemistry\nQuantum Security & Cryptography\nQuantum AI & Software\nOpen Quantum Innovation\n\nPPT Template for Hackathon:\n[PPT TEMPLATE\n](https://canva.link/b51hvxu95kmz95f)\nNote- Make a copy of the template before editing.\n\n**Important**\n* Solo participation is not permitted. Teams must consist of 3–4 members.\n* All team members must register individually on Devfolio.\n* Teams must be formed on Devfolio before submitting their Round 1 project.\n* Only the Team Lead should submit the Round 1 project submission form on behalf of the team.\n* The Round 1 submission must include the required idea ppt, Demo Video, Minimal Prototype, and GitHub Repository.\n\nSubmit your team's project here:\n[ROUND 1 PROJECT SUBMISSION](https://www.quantumweek.tech/hackathon/submission)\n\n**Deadline:** 10 October 2026, 11:59 PM IST\n\n**Results & Further Updates**\n\nRound 1 results will be announced on 12 October 2026.\nThe Top 30 teams shortlisted from Round 1 will participate in the Round 2 Enhancement Sprint and subsequently attend the Grand Finale at Ramaiah Institute of Technology on 30–31 October 2026.",
