      "description": "# **About Realm Hack '26**\n\n**Realm Hack '26** is the flagship annual hackathon organized by CFRA — Computer Science Forum: Realm of Academics, College of Engineering Karunagappally. \n\nBuilt for students and independent developers across India, Realm Hack brings together builders, and problem-solvers to create impactful technology solutions. The hackathon is designed as a three-round selection process, ensuring every team is evaluated on both the quality of its idea and its technical execution before the on-campus finale. \n\nWhether you're building your first project or your next big startup idea, Realm Hack '26 is your opportunity to learn, collaborate, and compete on a national stage.\n\n### Hackathon Structure\n\n**Round 1 — Registration & Idea Submission**\n* Register your team on Devfolio and submit a project title, technology track, and a short abstract describing your idea.\n* Applications are reviewed for originality, problem relevance, innovation, feasibility, and potential impact.\n* Selected teams advance to Round 2 — Online Technical Evaluation.\n\n**Round 2 — Online Technical Evaluation**\n* Round 2 is conducted through the official Realm Hack website and is open only to teams shortlisted from Round 1.\n* Shortlisted teams will receive access to the Round 2 submission portal, where they can download the official 4-slide PPT template and submit their technical proposal before the submission deadline.\n* Submissions in this round are evaluated to shortlist teams for the Offline Grand Finale. \n* Teams shortlisted from Round 2 will receive an official invitation to compete in the Offline Grand Finale.\n\n**Round 3 — Offline Grand Finale**\n* Teams shortlisted from Round 2 will be invited to the Realm Hack '26 Grand Finale at the College of Engineering Karunagappally.\n* Finalists will participate in a 24-hour offline hackathon, build and present their solutions before an expert judging panel, connect with mentors and industry professionals, and compete for the ₹60,000 prize pool.\n\n### Who Can Participate?\n* Students from any college or university in India.\n* Individual developers and teams of 1–4 members.\n\n### Official Website\nFull rules, submission guidelines, announcements, and Round 2 updates will be available on the official website: [realmhack.in](https://realmhack.in)",
