      "description": "About Internwell Hack2.0\n\nInternwell Hack2.0 is a student-driven hackathon organized by Internwell-SLIET Club at Sant Longowal Institute of Engineering and Technology (SLIET), bringing together passionate students, developers, designers, innovators, and problem-solvers to turn ideas into impactful solutions.\n\nThe hackathon provides a platform for participants to build, experiment, collaborate, and learn by working on real-world challenges using technology. Whether you are an experienced developer or participating in your first hackathon, Internwell Hack2.0 encourages everyone to think creatively, explore new technologies, and build something meaningful.\n\n What to Expect\n\n- Build innovative solutions to real-world problems\n- Collaborate with teammates and learn from each other\n- Explore technologies such as AI, Web, Mobile, IoT, Blockchain, and more\n-  Compete, showcase your ideas, and get recognized\n-  Connect with fellow innovators, mentors, and the student tech community\n-  Gain practical experience beyond the classroom\n\n Our Vision\n\nInternwell Hack2.0 aims to create an environment where ideas become prototypes and prototypes become solutions. We believe that students can create meaningful technological solutions when given the right platform, community, and opportunity.\n\n🔥 Who Can Participate?\n\nStudents from SLIET and other institutions who are passionate about technology, innovation, problem-solving, and entrepreneurship are welcome to participate. Bring your ideas, form your team, and get ready to build!\n\nThink. Build. Innovate. Impact.\n\nWelcome to Internwell Hack2.0 — where the next generation of innovators starts building.",
