      "description": "**HackSpire'26 – The Flagship Hackathon of FIEM ACM Student Chapter**\n\nHackSpire is the flagship annual hackathon organized by the **FIEM ACM Student Chapter**, recognized as the **Most Active ACM Student Chapter in East India**. Following the tremendous success of our previous editions—including **4100+ registrations, 270 in-person participants, and 50+ innovative project submissions**—we are excited to announce **HackSpire'26**, set to be bigger, bolder, and more impactful than ever before.\n\nHackSpire brings together some of the brightest student innovators, developers, and creators from across the country for an intense **26-hour hackathon experience** filled with innovation, collaboration, and learning. Participants will work in teams to build solutions for real-world challenges while exploring cutting-edge technologies across multiple domains.\n\n### 📍 Event Details\n\n**Event:** HackSpire'26\n**Venue:** Future Institute of Engineering and Management, Kolkata\n**Duration:** 26 Hours of Innovation\n\n### Why join HackSpire'26?\n\n **Build innovative projects** across software and hardware tracks\n **Solve real-world problems** through curated problem statements\n **Learn from mentors and industry experts** through workshops and sessions\n **Network with developers, founders, and tech communities**\n **Win exciting prizes, swags, and recognition**\n\nAt HackSpire, we believe hackathons are not just about competition—they are about **collaboration, creativity, and community building**. Whether you are a beginner exploring your first hackathon or an experienced hacker ready to push boundaries, **HackSpire'26** provides the perfect platform to **learn, build, and showcase your ideas** at one of Kolkata’s most exciting student-led hackathons.",
