      "registrationStatus": "closed",
      "description": "researcher behind ChatGPT spent two years building a different kind of AI.\n\n​Come build with it.\n\n​**GODSPEED** is a four-hour build jam around Jev, T[ypeSafe AI’s newly released model](https://typesafe.ai/blog/introducing-system-one-models-and-jev?utm_source=luma) built for fast, structured decisions.\n\n​Instead of asking an AI model to generate a long answer and then figuring out what to do with it, Jev is designed to make small, specific decisions your software can act on.\n\n​Give it a situation. Ask it what should happen next. Get back a choice, score or probability. Then build around it.\n\n​The model launched only a few days ago, so the experiments are still wide open.\n\n## ​What can you build?\n\n​Give a game character an instinct.\n\n​Build an agent that knows when to stop.\n\n​Race Jev through Wikipedia.\n\n​Turn films, ideas or people into a live map of meaning.\n\n​Build something completely different.\n\n​There are no fixed problem statements.\n\n​The goal is simple:\n\n`​Your input → Jev makes a decision → Your software does something`\n\n​We’ll start by understanding the research and getting your [first Jev call](https://docs.typesafe.ai/) running.\n\n​Then you’ll form teams, pick an idea and build the smallest version people can actually use or play with.\n\n​At the end, everyone demos.\n\n## ​Agenda\n\n​12:00–12:20 PM — Meet Jev + understand the research\n12:20–12:40 PM — Make your first call, find teammates + choose a build\n12:40–2:20 PM — Build\n2:20–2:35 PM — Break + try other projects\n2:35–3:20 PM — Final build sprint\n3:20–4:00 PM — Demo time\n\n## ​Before you come\n\n​Read the [Jev launch post](https://typesafe.ai/blog/introducing-system-one-models-and-jev?utm_source=luma) if you want to understand the idea beforehand.\n\n​Explore the [Jev documentation](https://docs.typesafe.ai/?utm_source=luma) if you want to get a head start.\n\n​We’ve also put together the [GODSPEED Builder Guide](https://ai-weekend-godspeed.tushaar.chatgpt.site/) with build ideas, examples and everything you need for the jam.\n\n​Come solo or bring friends.\n\n​Bring your laptop, charger, coding environment and curiosity.\n\n​Godspeed.",
