      "registrationStatus": "closed",
      "description": "# **About NexHack 2.0**\n\n# **Introduction**\n\nWelcome to **NexHack 2.0, a 36-hour National-Level Hackathon** scheduled for **25th–26th September 2026**, bringing together some of the brightest student innovators from across the country.\n\n**📍 Venue: Institute of Information Technology & Management (IITM), D-29, Institutional Area, Janakpuri, New Delhi – 110058**\n\nNexHack 2.0 provides an exciting platform for participants to showcase their creativity, technical expertise, and problem-solving abilities by developing innovative, AI-driven solutions to real-world challenges. The hackathon is designed to foster innovation, collaboration, and technological excellence while empowering participants to transform bold ideas into impactful solutions.\n\nWhether you're an experienced hacker or participating in your first hackathon, NexHack 2.0 offers an opportunity to learn, build, network with like-minded innovators, receive mentorship, and compete for exciting rewards.\n\nJoin us for an inspiring journey of innovation, learning, and creation at NexHack 2.0!\n\n# **Who Can Participate?**\n\n* Students from all colleges and universities are welcome.\n* Teams must consist of 2–5 members.\n* Cross-disciplinary teams are encouraged to promote diverse perspectives and innovative solutions.\n* Beginners are highly encouraged to participate.\n\n# **Hackathon Journey**\n\n**Phase 1: Registration**\n\nRegister your team through Devfolio before the registration deadline.\n\n**Phase 2: Online Idea Presentation (5th September 2026)**\n\nAll registered teams will be invited to present their project idea during an **online evaluation session on 5th September 2026** before the mentor panel.\n\nDuring the presentation, teams should showcase:\n\n* Problem Statement\n* Proposed Solution\n* Technology Stack\n* Key Features\n* Expected Impact\n* Prototype Demonstration (recommended)\n* Future Scope and Vision\n\nTeams should be prepared for a short Q&A session where mentors may ask questions regarding the feasibility, technical approach, and scalability of the proposed solution.\n\n**Phase 3: Shortlisting**\n\nBased on the online presentations and evaluation, the highest-scoring teams will be shortlisted for the 36-hour offline Grand Finale.\n\n**Phase 4: Final Offline Hackathon (25th–26th September 2026)**\n\nShortlisted teams will participate in the **36-hour National-Level Hackathon on 25th–26th September 2026**, where they will build, refine, and enhance their solutions with guidance from mentors and industry experts.\n\n**Phase 5: Final Evaluation & Winner Announcement**\n\nTeams will demonstrate their working solutions before the judging panel. After evaluation, winners will be announced during the closing ceremony.\n\n# **Online Round Evaluation Criteria**\n\nProjects will be evaluated on the following parameters:\n\n* Innovation & Originality – 25%\n* Problem Relevance & Impact – 20%\n* Feasibility of the Proposed Solution – 20%\n* Technical Approach & Technology Stack – 15%\n* Clarity and Quality of Presentation – 10%\n* Scalability & Future Scope – 10%\n\nOnly the top-performing teams will advance to the final round.\n\n# **Final Evaluation Criteria**\n\nDuring the hackathon, judges will evaluate projects based on:\n\n* Innovation and Creativity\n* Technical Complexity\n* Functionality and Working Prototype\n* UI/UX Design\n* Real-world Impact\n* Presentation and Demonstration\n* Scalability\n* Business Potential (where applicable)\n\n# **🏆 Rewards & Recognition**\n\nParticipants at NexHack 2.0 won't just compete for prizes—they'll gain valuable experience, industry exposure, and opportunities to connect with the innovation ecosystem.\n\n* 💰 Prize Pool: INR 37,000+\n* 🎁 Swags, goodies, and participation certificates for all eligible participants.\n* 🍽️ Food and refreshments will be provided throughout the 36-hour offline hackathon.\n* 🛏️ Free accommodation for all shortlisted offline participants.\n* 🌐 Networking opportunities with industry experts, mentors, judges, and fellow innovators.\n* 🏅 Recognition across NexVerse platforms and our growing tech community.\n\nJoin us to compete, collaborate, learn, and transform your ideas into impactful solutions while earning recognition at one of the most exciting student hackathons of the year.\n\n# **Rules**\n\n* All work submitted and presented must be original and developed by the participating team.\n* Teams must adhere to the Hackathon Code of Conduct throughout the event.\n* Any form of plagiarism, misconduct, or unfair practices will result in immediate disqualification.\n* Participants are expected to maintain professionalism and respect towards fellow participants, mentors, judges, and organizers.\n* Teams must attend their scheduled online presentation. Failure to do so without prior approval may lead to disqualification.\n* The decision of the organizing committee and judging panel shall be final and binding.\n\n# **Why Participate?**\n\n* Solve real-world challenges using technology and AI.\n* Build impactful projects with like-minded innovators.\n* Receive mentorship from experienced professionals.\n* Expand your network with students and industry experts.\n* Win exciting prizes, certificates, and recognition.\n* Strengthen your portfolio with a nationally competitive hackathon project.\n\n# **Join the Community**\n\nTo connect with other participants, ask questions, discuss ideas, and form teams, join our WhatsApp Community:\n\n**WhatsApp Community:**\nhttps://chat.whatsapp.com/L8AhpeNEHOY1lai9KMdb8M\n\nImportant announcements and updates will be shared through email as well as the WhatsApp community, so make sure to stay connected and keep an eye on your inbox.\n\n**Think. Build. Innovate.**\n\n**Welcome to NexHack 2.0! 🚀**",
