      "description": "## About Binary Hacks 4.0\n\n**Binary Hacks 4.0** is a **36-hour offline hackathon** organized by **The Binary Club, Department of Computer Science & Engineering (CSE)**. The event brings together passionate developers, designers, and innovators to build impactful solutions for real-world challenges while fostering innovation, teamwork, and technical excellence.\n\nWhether you're a beginner or an experienced hacker, Binary Hacks 4.0 provides an exciting platform to collaborate with like-minded peers, learn from mentors, explore emerging technologies, and transform ideas into working prototypes.\n\nJoin us for **36 hours of coding, creativity, collaboration, and innovation**, compete for exciting cash prizes, and showcase your skills while connecting with fellow tech enthusiasts.\n\n**Event Details**\n\n* **Duration:** 36 Hours\n* **Dates:** 21–22 September\n* **Venue:** CRC Hall 1 & Hall 2\n* **Mode:** Offline\n* **Organizer:** The Binary Club, Department of Computer Science & Engineering (CSE)\n* **Perks:** Cash Prizes, Certificates for All Participants, Mentorship, Networking, and Swag",
