      "description": "<p><strong>Overview</strong></p>\n<p>PitchCraft 3.0 is a flagship ideathon organized as part of IEEE Days 2026. It provides a platform for students to develop innovative and feasible solutions to real-world problems and present their ideas before a judging panel. The event focuses on problem-solving, originality, feasibility, implementation, and impact.</p>\n<p><strong>Shortlisted Teams Announcement:</strong> 21st October 2026, 12:00 Noon</p>\n<p><strong>WhatsApp Group: </strong><a class=\"x1i10hfl xjbqb8w x1ejq31n x18oe1m7 x1sy0etr xstzfhl x972fbf x10w94by x1qhh985 x14e42zd x9f619 x1ypdohk xt0psk2 x3ct3a4 xdj266r x14z9mp xat24cr x1lziwak xexx8yu xyri2b x18d9i69 x1c1uobl x16tdsg8 xggy1nq x1a2a7pz xkrqix3 x1sur9pj x1s688f x7l2uk3 x1bvjpef x17kgsl5\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"link\" href=\"https://chat.whatsapp.com/Hhagq0zSN2JCktgN4Xrcnc?s=cl&amp;p=a&amp;mlu=4&amp;ilr=4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\">https://chat.whatsapp.com/Hhagq0zSN2JCktgN4Xrcnc?s=cl&amp;p=a&amp;mlu=4&amp;ilr=4</a></p>\n<h2>Guidelines:</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to all students from any college/university.</li>\n<li>Team size: <strong>2&ndash;4 members</strong>.</li>\n<li>Only registered team members will be allowed to present.</li>\n<li>Registration is compulsory through <strong>Unstop</strong>. No on-spot registration is allowed.</li>\n<li>Names must be entered exactly as per College ID.</li>\n<li>The PPT must include:\n<ul>\n<li>Team Name</li>\n<li>Selected Problem Statement</li>\n<li>Problem Explanation</li>\n<li>Proposed Solution</li>\n<li>Implementation Approach</li>\n<li>Feasibility</li>\n<li>Expected Impact</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>All work must be original. Plagiarism will result in disqualification.</li>\n<li>Shortlisted Teams will be declared on the whatsApp group and the registered email of the leader.</li>\n<li>Registration fees of 100rs will be collected for offline campus round after shortlisting in online ppt round.</li>\n<li>For further details join the whatsapp group.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Rules:</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Shortlisted teams must report 30 minutes prior at the venue.</li>\n<li>Teams must bring their own laptop and necessary accessories such as chargers and adapters.</li>\n<li>All team members must carry valid College ID cards.</li>\n<li>No substitutions or extra entries are allowed.</li>\n<li>Delay may lead to cancellation of the presentation slot.</li>\n<li>Participants must respect the allotted time limits.</li>\n<li>Any misconduct may lead to disqualification.</li>\n<li>Judges' decision will be final and binding.</li>\n</ul>",
