      "id": "unstop:1769462",
      "slug": "unstop-fallout",
      "source": "unstop",
      "sourceEventId": "1769462",
      "sourceUrl": "https://unstop.com/hackathons/fallout-university-school-of-automation-robotics-usar-guru-gobind-singh-indraprastha-university-ggsipu-delhi-1769462",
      "title": "Fallout",
      "organizer": {
        "name": "University School of Automation & Robotics (USAR) ,Guru Gobind Singh Indraprastha University (GGSIPU), Delhi",
        "trustScore": 88,
        "pastEventCount": 3
      },
      "type": "hackathon",
      "mode": "offline",
      "city": "East Delhi",
      "venue": "East Delhi",
      "startsAt": "2026-10-13 01:48:54 GMT+0530",
      "endsAt": "2026-10-21T16:00:00+05:30",
      "registrationClosesAt": "2026-10-21T16:00:00+05:30",
      "registrationStatus": "open",
      "description": "<p><strong>About Fallout</strong></p>\n<p>Fallout is an on-site structural design challenge by SAE USAR, part of Elysian 2026. Every team gets the same kit, the same 2.5 hours and one job: build a bridge that carries the most load for the least weight. Then every bridge is loaded until it fails. Everything fails eventually. The only question is how much it carried first.</p>\n<p><strong>Event Details</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Date: 21 October 2026</li>\n<li>Time: 1:00 PM &ndash; 4:00 PM (approx.)</li>\n<li>Venue: A-302 | Materials Lab, University School of Automation &amp; Robotics, GGSIPU East Delhi Campus, Delhi</li>\n<li>Mode: Offline</li>\n<li>Registration fee: Free</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility &amp; Team Formation</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Open to all college students, any year, any branch, any college.</li>\n<li>Individual and team participation allowed, with a maximum of 3 members per team.</li>\n<li>Inter-college and inter-branch teams are permitted.</li>\n<li>All participants must register on Unstop before 19 October 2026, 11:59 PM.</li>\n<li>Carry your college ID on the day.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>How Fallout Works</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Briefing:</strong> Rules, the kit and the test setup are explained.</li>\n<li><strong>Build (2.5 hours):</strong> Design and build your bridge on the spot. The design is entirely up to you: truss, arch, beam, anything, as long as it spans the test gap.</li>\n<li><strong>Weigh-in:</strong> Each finished bridge is weighed.</li>\n<li><strong>Load test:</strong> Each bridge is placed across the supports and loaded gradually with weights until it fails.</li>\n<li><strong>Result:</strong> The bridge with the best load-to-mass ratio wins.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Test Setup</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The gap between supports is the same for every team and will be announced at the briefing.</li>\n<li>Load is applied gradually, and the load held is measured on a weighing balance.</li>\n<li><strong>Failure</strong> means the bridge breaks and the weights fall.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Scoring</strong></p>\n<p>Score = maximum load supported before failure &divide; mass of your bridge. The highest ratio wins. Strong isn't enough. A light bridge that carries the same load beats a heavy one.</p>\n<p><strong>Materials &amp; Tools</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Materials, joining material and tools are provided by the organizers.</li>\n<li>Every team gets an identical kit. Details are shared at the briefing.</li>\n<li>Do not bring your own materials, tools or pre-built parts.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Maximum 3 members per team.</li>\n<li>The bridge must be built entirely on-site, during the build window, using only the provided kit.</li>\n<li>Pre-built or pre-cut components are not allowed.</li>\n<li>Bridges must be submitted when the build time ends. No modifications after that.</li>\n<li>A bridge that cannot span the test gap cannot be tested and scores zero.</li>\n<li>Tools are to be used safely and as instructed by the organizers.</li>\n<li>During load testing, everyone stays behind the marked safety line. Bridges fail suddenly.</li>\n<li>Organizers' decisions are final.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>What You Get</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Certificates</li>\n<li>Refreshments during the event</li>\n<li>All materials and tools provided</li>\n<li>A live look at how your design actually behaves under load</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Stay Connected</strong></p>\n<p>Join the Fallout '26 WhatsApp group for announcements: <a href=\"https://chat.whatsapp.com/K97iFP5CTMFIbYZ35FC8SX\">Fallout '26</a></p>",
      "eligibility": "{\"sector\":[\"students\"],\"engineering\":[],\"bSchools\":[],\"arts\":[],\"medicine\":[],\"law\":[],\"others\":[\"all\"],\"experience\":[\"all\"],\"studentPassoutYearsSelected\":[\"all\"],\"fresherPassoutYearsSelected\":[\"all\"],\"schoolFilteredClasses\":[\"all\"],\"minMarks\":{\"high_school_perc\":0,\"high_school_cgpa\":0},\"locations\":[],\"location_type\":\"all\",\"professionalEligibility\":null,\"fresherEligibility\":null}",
