      "description": "<p><strong>Overview</strong></p>\n<p>Kurukshetra &mdash; Where Ideas Meet Innovation is a technology and innovation event organized by Devkraft &times; CSI, Dr. D. Y. Patil Institute of Technology, Pimpri, Pune.</p>\n<p>The event brings together students, technology enthusiasts, and industry professionals to encourage innovation, collaboration, and problem-solving.</p>\n<p>Kurukshetra begins with Technical Inauguration, a podcast-style technical interaction featuring industry professionals who share their real-world experiences, career journeys, and industry insights. This is followed by an exciting 24-hour hackathon, where participants collaborate to develop innovative solutions to real-world challenges.</p>\n<p>Join us to learn, build, collaborate, and turn your ideas into impactful solutions!</p>\n<p><strong>Event Details</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Event Name: Kurukshetra 2026</li>\n<li>Organizers: Devkraft &times; CSI</li>\n<li>Registration Fees: Rs 799/-</li>\n<li>Registration Website: https://www.kurukshetradypdpu.in/</li>\n<li>Institution: Dr. D. Y. Patil Institute of Technology, Pimpri, Pune</li>\n<li>Event Dates: 16&ndash;17 October 2026</li>\n<li>Venue: DPU Auditorium and college campus, Dr. D. Y. Patil Institute of Technology, Pimpri, Pune</li>\n<li>Format: Technical Inauguration followed by a 24-hour hackathon</li>\n<li>Expected Participation: Approximately 1,200 participants and 200 teams across the event</li>\n<li>Hackathon Duration: 24 hours</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility Criteria</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The hackathon is open to college and university students.</li>\n<li>Each team must consist of 2&ndash;4 members.</li>\n<li>Inter-College and inter-branch teams are allowed.</li>\n<li>All participants must complete registration through the official Unstop listing.</li>\n<li>Participants must bring their own laptops and any other equipment required for development.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Hackathon Format</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Phase 1: Registration</strong></p>\n<p>Participants can access the official Kurukshetra registration website through the Unstop listing. Teams must consist of 2&ndash;4 students from the same institution.</p>\n<p><strong>Phase 2: Technical Inauguration</strong></p>\n<p>Participants attend Technical Inauguration, featuring industry professionals sharing their experiences, insights, and career guidance.</p>\n<p><strong>Phase 3: Problem Statement Announcement</strong></p>\n<p>The official hackathon problem statements will be announced at the end of Technical Inauguration.</p>\n<p>Participants will receive the problem statements and relevant instructions from the organizing committee. Teams can then select or work on the designated challenge according to the official guidelines.</p>\n<p>Number of problem statements: To be announced by the organizers.</p>\n<p><strong>Phase 4: 24-Hour Development</strong></p>\n<p>Teams will have 24 hours to brainstorm, design, develop, test, and refine their solutions. Participants are expected to collaborate effectively and manage their time throughout the challenge.</p>\n<p><strong>Phase 5: Final Submission and Presentation</strong></p>\n<p>At the end of the 24-hour development period, teams must submit their projects according to the organizers' instructions and present their solutions to the judging panel.</p>\n<p>Submission format, presentation duration, and evaluation schedule: To be announced by the organizers.</p>\n<p><strong>Rules and Regulations</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Each team must contain 2&ndash;4 members from the same college or university.</li>\n<li>Students from different college or branches may form a team.</li>\n<li>Each participant may register with only one team.</li>\n<li>Teams must work on the official problem statements announced at the end of Technical Inauguration.</li>\n<li>Solutions must be developed within the official 24-hour hackathon duration.</li>\n<li>Participants must bring their own laptops and ensure their development environment is ready.</li>\n<li>Projects must be original. Pre-existing code, open-source libraries, APIs, and third-party tools may be used where appropriate, provided their use is properly acknowledged.</li>\n<li>Plagiarism, misrepresentation, or copying another team's work may result in disqualification.</li>\n<li>Teams must submit their projects before the deadline specified by the organizing committee.</li>\n<li>Teams must comply with the submission, presentation, and technical guidelines communicated by the organizers.</li>\n<li>Participants must maintain discipline and follow the rules of the venue and event.</li>\n<li>The organizing committee reserves the right to address rule violations and resolve disputes in accordance with the event guidelines.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Judging Criteria</strong></p>\n<p>Projects may be evaluated on the following parameters:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Innovation and Creativity: Originality and uniqueness of the proposed solution.</li>\n<li>Technical Implementation: Quality, functionality, and effective use of technology.</li>\n<li>Problem-Solving: How effectively the solution addresses the selected problem statement.</li>\n<li>Feasibility and Impact: Practical applicability, scalability, and potential real-world impact.</li>\n<li>Presentation and Demonstration: Clarity of the project explanation and effectiveness of the final demonstration.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Final judging criteria and weightage: To be announced by the organizers.</p>\n<p><strong>Registration Process</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Visit the official Kurukshetra listing on Unstop.</li>\n<li>Click the registration link to be redirected to the official Kurukshetra website.</li>\n<li>Complete the registration process on the website by providing the required participant and team details.</li>\n<li>Form a team of 2&ndash;4 students from the same college or university.</li>\n<li>Follow the instructions provided by the organizing committee to complete registration.</li>\n<li>Stay updated through official communication channels for event updates and further instructions.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Important Instructions</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Participants must follow the official schedule and instructions issued by the organizing committee.</li>\n<li>The problem statements will be revealed at the end of Technical Inauguration.</li>\n<li>Teams are responsible for bringing their own laptops and required development equipment.</li>\n<li>Teams should ensure that their projects are ready for demonstration at the end of the 24-hour period.</li>\n<li>Details concerning internet access, accommodation, meals, certificates, prizes, and intellectual property will be communicated by the organizers once finalized.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Be Part of Kurukshetra!</strong></p>\n<p>Learn from industry professionals at Technical Inauguration, discover the hackathon challenges, collaborate with talented peers, and challenge yourself to build something meaningful in 24 hours.</p>\n<p>Bring your ideas. Build with your team. Innovate at Kurukshetra.</p>\n<p>Organized by Devkraft &times; CSI</p>",
