      "description": "<p><strong>About the Event</strong></p>\n<p>EchelonHacks Young Innovators 2026 is an inter-school hackathon hosted by Echelon Institute of Technology, Faridabad (Dept. of Computer Science &amp; Engineering). It gives school students a chance to turn ideas into working prototypes and present them to industry mentors and judges.<br /><br />Website: Submission&nbsp;<br />Will be updated soon</p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>School students of Class 9th, 10th , 11th, 12th</li>\n<li>Team size: [2-4] members, all from the same school</li>\n<li>Registration through Unstop</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Format</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li><strong>Round 1 (Online):</strong> Teams submit a short idea presentation (5 slides) and a 1-2 minute demo video. Coding is not compulsory; simple prototypes are welcome. Problem statements will be shared when the online round begins.</li>\n<li><strong>Round 2 (Offline Finale):</strong> Top shortlisted teams build and present their prototypes at the Echelon campus in a 9-hour on-site round, with mentor support, lunch and a final 5-minute pitch.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Timeline</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Registration: 12 Oct - 30 Oct 2026</li>\n<li>Online Round: 31 Oct - 5 Nov 2026</li>\n<li>Results: 10 Nov 2026</li>\n<li>Offline Finale: 21 Nov 2026, 9:00 AM - 6:00 PM, Echelon Institute of Technology, Faridabad</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Judging Criteria</strong><br />Idea and Innovation, Technical Feasibility, Real-World Impact, Presentation</p>\n<p><strong>Rules</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"ltr\">\n<li>Work must be original; plagiarism leads to disqualification</li>\n<li>AI tools may be used for learning, but the team must be able to explain its own work</li>\n<li>Shortlisted teams must submit a parent/guardian consent form and be accompanied by a teacher or guardian on finale day</li>\n<li>Judges&rsquo; decisions are final</li>\n</ul>",
