      "registrationStatus": "open",
      "description": "<p><strong>Tech Fusion-2026 | Vaish College of Engineering, Rohtak</strong></p>\n<h2>About the Competition</h2>\n<p>A server is broken, the application is failing, and the evidence is waiting to be discovered. Who caused the crash?</p>\n<p>Server Crash is a hands-on debugging challenge that tests participants' programming, troubleshooting, and server investigation skills.</p>\n<h2>Eligibility and Team Size</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Team size: 1- 4 members.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Participants must bring their own laptops.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Programming languages: Java or Python.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Competition Format</h2>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Find the Bug</strong><br />Teams receive a broken application or server setup containing intentional problems. Examples include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Incorrect configuration</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>API failure</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Database connection issues</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Port-related problems</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Code bugs</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Authentication failures</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Teams must identify the issue and explain its cause.</p>\n<p><strong>Round 2: Debug the Server</strong><br />Teams investigate a malfunctioning application, identify the underlying problem, and attempt to fix it. Every team receives the same problem and environment.</p>\n<p>Internet access and external resources will be restricted or permitted according to the organizers' instructions.</p>\n<h2>Rules</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Bring your own laptop and be prepared to work in Java or Python.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Follow the debugging environment and resource restrictions announced by the organizers.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Do not interfere with other teams or unauthorized systems.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>Explain your findings and demonstrate your solution as instructed.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Find the bug. Diagnose the failure. Bring the server back to life.</p>",
