      "registrationClosesAt": "2026-12-09T23:59:55+05:30",
      "registrationStatus": "open",
      "description": "<p><strong>Code Quest 2026 &mdash; Ready. Set. Code.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Code Quest 2026</strong> is a competitive programming event designed to test participants' programming fundamentals, problem-solving abilities, logical reasoning, and Data Structures and Algorithms (DSA) skills.</p>\n<p>The competition consists of two rounds, progressing from a fast-paced multiple-choice quiz to a hands-on coding challenge. Participants will compete individually, solve problems under time constraints, and demonstrate their ability to think logically and write efficient solutions.</p>\n<p>Whether you're confident in programming fundamentals or ready to challenge yourself with DSA, Code Quest is an opportunity to put your skills to the test.</p>\n<p><strong>Competition Format</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Round 1: MCQ Sprint</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Mode:</strong> Online quiz using Google Forms</li>\n<li><strong>Duration:</strong> 15 minutes</li>\n<li><strong>Total questions:</strong> 15 multiple-choice questions</li>\n<li><strong>Marks per question:</strong> 10 points</li>\n<li><strong>Maximum score:</strong> 150 points</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Topics covered:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Data Structures and Algorithms fundamentals</li>\n<li>Python programming</li>\n<li>Programming fundamentals</li>\n<li>Logical reasoning related to programming</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Participants must answer the questions within the allotted time. This round tests conceptual understanding, accuracy, and speed.</p>\n<p><strong>Round 2: DSA Challenge</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Mode:</strong> Online coding contest on Hackerrank</li>\n<li><strong>Duration:</strong> 1 hour 45 minutes</li>\n<li><strong>Total problems:</strong> 4</li>\n<li><strong>Maximum score:</strong> 1,050 points</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Participants will solve four coding problems of increasing difficulty.</p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<th>Difficulty</th>\n<th>Number of problems</th>\n<th>Points</th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Easy</td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>150 + 200</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Medium</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>300</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Hard</td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>400</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Total</strong></td>\n<td><strong>4</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1,050</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>This round evaluates coding ability, algorithmic thinking, problem-solving skills, and the ability to develop solutions that satisfy the given test cases.</p>\n<p><strong>Eligibility</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The competition is open to students interested in programming, Python, and problem-solving.</li>\n<li>Participants should have a basic understanding of programming fundamentals.</li>\n<li>Familiarity with Data Structures and Algorithms is recommended for Round 2.</li>\n<li>Participants must have access to a stable internet connection and a device capable of running a modern web browser.</li>\n<li>Participants must have a HackerRank account.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Participation Format</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The competition is conducted on an individual basis.</li>\n<li>Each participant must register using their own details.</li>\n<li>Participants must use their own registered account or identity when attempting the competition.</li>\n<li>Team participation is not applicable.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Competition Rules</strong></p>\n<ol start=\"1\">\n<li><strong>Independent solving only:</strong> Participants must solve all questions independently.</li>\n<li><strong>No external assistance:</strong> The use of AI assistants, AI code generators, online solution repositories, external websites for solving questions, or communication with other participants for answers is prohibited during the contest.</li>\n<li><strong>No plagiarism:</strong> Copying or sharing solutions with other participants is not permitted.</li>\n<li><strong>Fair play:</strong> Participants must not exploit platform vulnerabilities, manipulate submissions, or use unauthorized methods to gain an unfair advantage.</li>\n<li><strong>Time limits:</strong> Participants must complete each round within its allotted duration.</li>\n<li><strong>Authentic participation:</strong> Participants must not impersonate another person or participate using multiple identities to gain an unfair advantage.</li>\n<li><strong>Platform compliance:</strong> Participants must follow the applicable rules and terms of HackerRank.</li>\n<li><strong>Disqualification:</strong> Organizers reserve the right to disqualify participants found violating the competition rules, subject to review of the available evidence.</li>\n<li><strong>Organizer's decision:</strong> Decisions made by the organizing team regarding rule violations and competition administration will be final.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Scoring and Results</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Round 1 carries a maximum of 150 points.</li>\n<li>Round 2 carries a maximum of 1,050 points.</li>\n<li>The maximum combined score is <strong>1,200 points</strong>.</li>\n<li>Final rankings will be determined using the combined scores from both rounds, provided both rounds are completed as part of the official competition format.</li>\n<li>In case of a tie, the organizers may use Round 2 score and then the time taken or submission performance in the coding round as tie-breakers, where reliable platform data is available.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Important Instructions</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Participants should carefully read all instructions before starting each round.</li>\n<li>Ensure a stable internet connection and log in to the required platforms in advance.</li>\n<li>Submit responses and coding solutions before the respective deadlines.</li>\n<li>The organizers will communicate the official links and any additional instructions through the designated event channels.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Get ready to test your skills, solve challenging problems, and compete in Code Quest 2026!</strong></p>\n<p>Ready. Set. Code.</p>",
