      "registrationClosesAt": "2026-10-24T00:00:00+05:30",
      "registrationStatus": "open",
      "description": "<p><strong>Overview</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Date:</strong> 13 October 2026<br /><strong>Venue:</strong> IT Lab</p>\n<p>The coding event will consist of two compulsory rounds.</p>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Debugging</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Duration:</strong> 45 minutes</li>\n<li><strong>Questions:</strong> 2 Easy, 1 Medium, 1 Hard</li>\n<li>Participants will be given erroneous code and must identify and fix the errors.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Round 2: Coding</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Duration:</strong> 60 minutes</li>\n<li><strong>Questions:</strong> 2 Easy, 1 Medium, 1 Hard</li>\n<li>Participants must write their own code to solve the given problems.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Sample Questions</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Sample questions will be shared with participants <strong>two days before the event</strong>.</li>\n<li>Event questions may be based on the samples, with slight modifications. They will not be completely different from the provided samples.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Programming Languages: </strong>Participants may use <strong>Java, C/C++, Go, or Python</strong>.</p>\n<p><strong>Test Cases</strong></p>\n<p>Each question will have five test cases:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>1 sample test case</li>\n<li>2 visible test cases</li>\n<li>2 hidden test cases</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Evaluation Criteria</strong></p>\n<p>Participants will be evaluated based on:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Score obtained for each question.</li>\n<li>Number of questions attempted.</li>\n<li>Time taken to solve each question.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The best submission for each question will be considered for evaluation.</p>\n<p><strong>Rules and Restrictions</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Both rounds are compulsory.</li>\n<li>Each round has its own global timer.</li>\n<li>The use of AI tools, internet access, and external assistance is strictly prohibited.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Give it your best, challenge yourself, and aim for the top. Good luck to everyone participating!</p>",
