      "description": "<p><strong>PITCH//BREAK: THE SURVIVAL ARENA</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Build under pressure. Bid for power. Adapt to the unexpected. Then defend your solution.</strong></p>\n<p>Pitch//Break is a two-day competition where teams build a solution, earn and spend points, adapt to challenges, and face off against rival teams. Every decision matters: earn points through your performance, use Power Cards strategically, and avoid faults that cost you points. The team with the highest score at the end wins.</p>\n<p><strong>Event timeline</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Day 1 &middot; 21 October</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Round 1: Initial Solution Build</strong><br />Submit your team&rsquo;s initial solution. This gives the judges a starting point for your team&rsquo;s journey in the arena.</p>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Round 2: Power Card Auction</strong> &mdash; Bid with your existing points to acquire Power Cards. Choose carefully: the right card could change your game.</li>\n<li><strong>Round 3: Challenge</strong> &mdash; Adapt your solution to a new challenge. Show the judges how well your team can think on its feet.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Day 2 &middot; 22 October</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Round 4: New Solution Pitch</strong> &mdash; Present your solution to the judges and earn points for your pitch.</li>\n<li><strong>Round 5: Sponsor Challenge</strong> &mdash; Take on a sponsor-led mini quiz or challenge to earn more points.</li>\n<li><strong>Final Round: Team vs Team</strong> &mdash; Surviving teams are paired to challenge each other&rsquo;s solutions and pitches. Use any Power Cards you have. Judges decide the winner of each face-off; faults or failures in your solution cost points.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>The team with the most points wins.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>What&rsquo;s at stake?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>₹50,000 prize pool</strong></li>\n<li><strong>2 remote internship opportunities</strong></li>\n<li>Swag and certificates for participants</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Event details</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Dates:</strong> 21&ndash;22 October 2026<br /><strong>Venue:</strong> A005 Lecture Hall, USAR &middot; GGSIPU East Delhi Campus<br /><strong>Team size:</strong> 1&ndash;4 members</p>\n<p>Bring a team that can build, adapt, pitch, and hold its ground. <strong>Register now and enter the arena.</strong></p>",
