      "description": "<p>BugWars is a <strong>high-energy coding challenge </strong>focused on <strong>debugging</strong>, <strong>problem</strong>-<strong>solving</strong>, and programming skills. Participants will tackle a range of coding problems designed to test their ability to identify errors, analyze logic, optimize solutions, and think under pressure. Covering concepts from <strong>DSA</strong> and <strong>Competitive Programming</strong>, the event challenges participants to turn broken code into efficient, working solutions.&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>Participation is individual-only, making it a fair and thrilling competition for all coders and debuggers</strong></p>\n<p><strong>What we're looking for:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Problem Solving</strong>: Strong logical and analytical thinking</li>\n<li><strong>Debugging Skills</strong>: Identifying and fixing errors efficiently</li>\n<li><strong>DSA &amp; CP</strong>: Familiarity with core concepts and algorithms</li>\n<li><strong>Code Optimization</strong>: Improving solutions for efficiency and performance</li>\n<li><strong>Attention to Detail</strong>: Spotting logical, syntactical, and runtime errors</li>\n<li><strong>Competitive Mindset</strong>: Ability to solve problems under time constraints&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Solo participation</li>\n<li>The contest will last for 2 hours</li>\n<li>There will be 3 winners in the contest</li>\n<li>The exact format and the platforms will be revealed then and there</li>\n<li>Participants must strictly avoid cheating, plagiarism, or using AI tools/assistants &mdash; violations will lead to immediate disqualification.</li>\n<li>Goodies, prizes, and certificates will be awarded to winners of each mini game.</li>\n<li>Participation Certificates will be awarded to all participants&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>",
