      "description": "<p data-pm-slice=\"1 1 []\">The system is under attack. Logic is your weapon. Algorithms are your ammunition. Only the fastest minds will survive.</p>\n<p>Welcome to <strong>CODE RED</strong>, the ultimate Competitive Programming Contest at <strong>XORDIUM 5.0</strong>, the technical fest of Birla Institute of Technology (BIT), Mesra, Patna Campus. Step into a cyberpunk-inspired digital battleground where every second counts, every submission matters, and every bug could cost you the leaderboard.</p>\n<p>Gear up to decode complex problems, optimize your algorithms, and outsmart competing coders in a high-intensity battle of logic, speed, and precision. The countdown is ticking. The terminal is live. <strong>Will you rise above the chaos?</strong></p>\n<p><strong>ENTER THE GRID. BREAK THE CODE. DOMINATE THE SYSTEM.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>All That You Need to Know About CODE RED</strong></p>\n<p><strong>CODE RED</strong> is a competitive programming contest designed to challenge participants' algorithmic thinking, data structures knowledge, coding speed, and problem-solving abilities. Hosted as part of <strong>XORDIUM 5.0 at BIT Mesra, Patna Campus</strong>, the contest welcomes passionate programmers ready to test their skills against talented coders.</p>\n<p>Whether you're a seasoned competitive programmer or an aspiring algorithmic problem-solver, this is your chance to enter the arena and prove your coding prowess.</p>\n<p><strong>Contest Details</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Event Name:</strong> CODE RED &mdash; Competitive Programming Contest</li>\n<li><strong>Fest:</strong> XORDIUM 5.0</li>\n<li><strong>Organized By:</strong> Birla Institute of Technology (BIT), Mesra, Patna Campus</li>\n<li><strong>Event Type:</strong> Competitive Programming</li>\n<li><strong>Participation:</strong> Individual</li>\n<li><strong>Mode:</strong> Online</li>\n<li><strong>Platform:</strong> Unstop</li>\n<li><strong>Duration:</strong> 1.5 Hours</li>\n<li><strong>Date &amp; Time: 25 Oct 2026 7:30PM to 11:30 PM</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Registration Deadline:</strong> 24 oct 2026</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Eligibility</strong></p>\n<p>The contest is open to students passionate about programming and problem-solving.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Undergraduate Students</li>\n<li>Postgraduate Students</li>\n<li>Engineering and Technology Students</li>\n<li>Students from Management, Science, Commerce, Arts, Law, and other disciplines</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Individual participation only.</strong> No teams. No shortcuts. Just you, your code, and the clock.</p>\n<p><strong>Rules &amp; Regulations</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The contest will feature algorithmic and data-structure-based programming problems.</li>\n<li>Participants must solve and submit their solutions within the allotted contest duration.</li>\n<li>Participants must register through Unstop and follow the official contest instructions.</li>\n<li>Plagiarism, copied submissions, or the use of multiple accounts to gain an unfair advantage may result in disqualification.</li>\n<li>Participants must comply with the contest platform's rules and the organizers' instructions.</li>\n<li>Rankings will be determined using the contest platform's scoring and tie-breaking rules.</li>\n<li>The organizing team's decision regarding contest administration and disputes will be final.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Process &amp; Format</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Step 1 &mdash; Register:</strong> Sign up for CODE RED through Unstop.</li>\n<li><strong>Step 2 &mdash; Gear Up:</strong> Review the contest guidelines and ensure your coding environment is ready.</li>\n<li><strong>Step 3 &mdash; Enter the Grid:</strong> Join the online contest during the officially announced time window.</li>\n<li><strong>Step 4 &mdash; Solve &amp; Survive:</strong> Tackle algorithmic challenges, submit optimized solutions, and climb the leaderboard.</li>\n<li><strong>Step 5 &mdash; Claim Your Glory:</strong> Top performers will be recognized according to the officially announced results and prize structure.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Prizes &amp; Recognition</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Exciting prizes for top-performing participants.</li>\n<li>Certificates of merit for eligible winners.</li>\n<li>Participation certificates, subject to the organizers' announced criteria.</li>\n<li>A chance to showcase your problem-solving skills and competitive programming abilities.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><em>Prize amounts, certificate eligibility, and distribution details will be announced by the organizing team.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Why Participate?</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Test Your Limits:</strong> Challenge your DSA, algorithms, and logical reasoning skills.</li>\n<li><strong>Race Against Time:</strong> Solve problems under pressure and make every submission count.</li>\n<li><strong>Climb the Leaderboard:</strong> Compete with programmers from across institutions.</li>\n<li><strong>Earn Recognition:</strong> Showcase your abilities through your contest performance.</li>\n<li><strong>Experience the Cyberpunk Arena:</strong> Become part of the high-energy technical atmosphere of XORDIUM 5.0.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>The Final Transmission</strong></p>\n<p>The network is unstable. The countdown has begun. The leaderboard awaits its next champion.</p>\n<p>One coder. One terminal. Zero excuses.</p>",
